.Dd October 22, 2026
.Dt PATINA-SETTINGS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-settings
.Nd the Patina desktop's Settings
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -page Ar page
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the desktop's Settings window, for what needs more than the desktop's
menu.
Its pages:
.Bl -tag -width "Night Light"
.It Appearance
The skin every piece of the shell wears, and its skins folder; the style,
Default, Light or Dark, that apps following the desktop take, GNOME's
.Ic color-scheme
setting; and the icon theme Files and GTK apps draw
with, GNOME's
.Ic icon-theme
setting for now, Yaru when it names none that's installed.
.It HUD
What the window tabs show (icons, titles, or both), which edge the bar sits
on, and its layout: one bar, or split into its parts (experimental), each placed by
dragging it on a map of the screen, where it snaps to the nearest spot, or
from a list.
Gaps around tiled windows and the bar, with how big they are and how round the
floating bar's corners are, written to
.Ic [gaps]
in the compositor's config.
Shadows: whether the desktop draws the ones Patina apps ask for around windows,
written to
.Ic [shadows]
in the same, and whether the HUD's parts have shadows and how they look (size,
opacity, drop, sideways offset, spread and colour).
Its config file is for everything else.
.It Wallpaper
The default, and the images in
.Pa ~/Pictures/Wallpapers
and the system's backgrounds.
.It Account
Your picture, shown on the lock screen: the Sector F flask in each skin's
colours, an image from
.Pa ~/Pictures/Avatars ,
or any picture chosen with the file chooser, written to
.Pa ~/.face .
.It Defaults
The app that opens links and each kind of file: the web browser, email,
calendar, folders, images, documents, text, music, video and archives,
each chosen from the installed apps that take it.
A choice is saved in
.Pa ~/.config/patina/defaults.toml
and written out as
.Pa ~/.config/patina-mimeapps.list ,
which
.Xr xdg-open 1
follows at once, in this desktop only.
Each row shows the app that opens it now.
.It Keyboard
The keyboard layouts Ctrl+Space steps through, in order: each moved up or
down, removed, or switched to, and more added from those XKB offers, found
by name, up to four, the most a keyboard holds; any past the fourth are
shown as not used.
And how soon and how fast a held key repeats.
While the compositor's config has no layouts it shows the system's, from
.Pa /etc/default/keyboard ,
and the first change copies them into
.Ic [keyboard] .
Changing the list goes back to the first layout.
.It Dictation
The key held to dictate, from the compositor's
.Ic [keys] ,
then, in
.Xr patina-dictate 1 Ns 's
config: the speech model, chosen from a short list and downloaded here (with
.Xr curl 1 ) ,
the language, the accuracy settings (search width, silence threshold, retrying
unsure passages, threads, and words to expect), and whether the overlay shows at
the bottom or the top of the screen.
.It Clipboard
Whether the desktop keeps a history of what's copied, how many copies, for how long, and whether
screenshots are put on the clipboard, in the compositor's
.Ic [clipboard] ;
and Clear history.
.It Displays
The connected monitors drawn to scale, to drag to the side of another they sit
on (or choose from menus), whether the desktop extends across them, mirrors, or
runs on the primary alone, and any monitor connected but off, with buttons to
extend or mirror onto it.
A monitor never placed before is marked.
Below them are the saved displays: each one placed is remembered, and a monitor
of the same model plugged in later goes where one was put, so a desk's monitors
come up in place, switched on without asking; Ask when plugged in brings the
popup back for one; the ones no connected monitor goes by are grayed, and Forget
removes one.
It's the compositor's
.Ql com.sectorflabs.Patina.Displays ,
so it works on the hardware only.
.It Night Light
Off, always on, or on a schedule, and how warm.
It shows whether this screen can be warmed, whether it's on now, with a
button to turn it off until the schedule next changes, and which apps are
holding it off.
.It Power and Battery
When the screen turns off without input, from never to 15 minutes, and
whether that locks it; and the power modes this machine has, through
power-profiles-daemon, why performance is held back, and which apps hold
a mode.
On a machine with a battery, then the battery: its charge, how much of
its original capacity it holds and its charge cycles, and graphs of its
charge and power draw over the last 24 hours or 7 days, shaded where it
was plugged in, from the history UPower keeps.
Hovering a graph reads out the time and value under the pointer.
.It Processes
What the compositor started: each one's state, PID, uptime and restarts,
with Restart and Stop.
A click on a name opens a window following its output.
Under
.Xr patina-session 1 ,
Restart Desktop restarts the compositor and everything with it, once
confirmed.
Settings can't restart itself.
.El
.Pp
Settings changes the files the settings live in, keeping the rest of each:
the bar's config for the skin and wallpaper, and
.Ic [night_light] ,
.Ic [gaps] ,
.Ic [shadows] ,
.Ic [screen]
and
.Ic [keyboard]
in the compositor's.
Those watching them change at once.
The monitors, Night Light's state, the layout in use and the processes come from the
compositor over the session bus; nested in another desktop, the pages say what isn't there.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -page Ar page
Open at
.Ar page :
.Cm appearance
(the default),
.Cm bar ,
.Cm wallpaper ,
.Cm defaults ,
.Cm keyboard ,
.Cm dictation ,
.Cm clipboard ,
.Cm displays ,
.Cm night-light ,
.Cm power
or
.Cm processes .
.It Fl h , -help
Print a short usage message.
.It Fl V , -version
Print the version.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/patina-hud/config.toml
.Ic skin ,
.Ic wallpaper
and
.Ic wallpaper_fit .
.It Pa ~/.config/patina-compositor/config.toml
.Ic [night_light] ,
.Ic [screen] off_after
and
.Ic [lock] on_screen_off .
.It Pa /usr/local/share/applications/com.sectorflabs.Settings.desktop
Its launcher entry, so the launcher and the bar know it by name and icon,
shown only on the Patina desktop;
.Ql make install
puts it there, with its icon in
.Pa /usr/local/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/ .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr patina-compositor 1 ,
.Xr patina-menu 1 ,
.Xr patina-night-light 1 ,
.Xr patina-desktop 7
